    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5dc59e3_441e2367",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1899057
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-06T16:52:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, Myles proposed using a fixed length array. Something like `@nullable byte[64] vendorControllerData\".\nI am a bit concerned with the padding, that can be sent outside the SoC, and can perhaps contain sensitive data. Moreover, this will not be uniform with standard commands that waits flexible amount of data.\nThe main concern of Myles, is that crash of the stack with a too big array. Do you know if we can limit the size of a \"byte[]\" by design?\nBy the way, I\u0027ve asked to QC if that fits, we can probably move forward with that.",
      "parentUuid": "e73b4a89_9e45c019",
      "revId": "71b6491ebe7b1d8397496071f723c6e69d4ec084",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a816b07_932c9a82",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T01:37:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think you should use a fixed-sized array. Resource exhaustion is possible with almost any type (String, vector, etc...). If you are worried about this, you should keep the length limit in framework code. Yeah?\n\nPlease also document on all of these fields that they should not be inspected in the framework, and document how they should be used (e.g.",
      "parentUuid": "b5dc59e3_441e2367",
      "revId": "71b6491ebe7b1d8397496071f723c6e69d4ec084",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dde202cd_e23535c1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T01:38:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "e.g. as opaque vendor data). Also, if you can name the types as \u0027vendorOpaqueData\u0027 or similar, that would be preferred, as how they should be used would be self-documenting, and it\u0027d be easier to see in framework code if they are inspected",
      "parentUuid": "0a816b07_932c9a82",
      "revId": "71b6491ebe7b1d8397496071f723c6e69d4ec084",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
